1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
 Well, we've reached the end of the course.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:08,780
 I hope that along the way, you learned not just how the internet works, but also gained

3
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:15,160
 a deeper appreciation for the decades of research, engineering, collaboration, and creativity

4
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:17,360
 that made it all possible.

5
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,080
 The modern internet can sometimes feel invisible.

6
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:23,160
 We use it every day.

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:29,900
 Packets move around the world, protocols coordinate billions of devices, routers, cables, servers,

8
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:36,960
 and software all work together so smoothly that we rarely stop to think about it.

9
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:41,320
 But underneath all of that is an extraordinary human story.

10
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:48,560
 A story of researchers, engineers, universities, governments, companies, and communities coming

11
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:52,240
 together and working together over many decades.

12
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:57,880
 And now, you understand a little more about how it all fits together.

13
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:02,000
 My hope is that this course gives you context.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,720
 Whether you become a software developer, a system administrator, a cybersecurity expert,

15
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:12,200
 or simply someone who wants to better understand the technology around them, understanding

16
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,440
 networking gives you a stronger foundation.

17
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:22,860
 And especially in the age of AI, understanding systems and context matters more than ever.

18
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:29,960
 Technology changes quickly, but the core ideas, packets, protocols, layering, standards, interoperability,

19
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:33,160
 human collaboration have stood the test of time.

20
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,360
 So thank you for spending this time with me.

21
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:38,680
 I hope you enjoyed the course, the interviews, and the stories.

22
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:44,720
 And I hope this course is just one step on a much longer journey of learning and exploration.

23
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:48,120
 Cheers, and I hope to see you in another course soon.

24
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:58,760
 [MUSIC PLAYING]

